<title>PHILIPPINES: Philippines' GrandAir to fly to the U.S..</title>
<headline>Philippines' GrandAir to fly to the U.S..</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippines Grand International Airways (GrandAir) said on Tuesday it was granted a permit to fly to the United States.</p>
<p>GrandAir chairman Dante Santos said the airline plans to fly regularly to Los Angeles via Honolulu.</p>
<p>&quot;Once we begin our services to the U.S., we will be looking for interline agreements with U.S. carriers,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>GrandAir is the second domestic airline allowed to ply regional and international routes. Earlier, Cebu Air Pacific was granted a permit to fly regional routes in Asia.</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom 63 2 8418939 fax 8176267</p>
